[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4459326618","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119474#issuecomment-4459326618","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119474","id":4459326618,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCcvsmg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T11:24:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-15T11:27:56Z","body":"I'm not sure this is a bug, the used resource is inside `res://` and shouldn't be overwritten there, and it's still linked to that instance from what I can see, when saving exported properties that hold external resources they are not saved themselves, to unlink it from the state you need to duplicate it, or save it manually in `user://`\n\nAlso, please note that your MRP contains the `.git` folder, which not only takes up unnecessary space but might leak private information","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4459326618/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4488890811","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119474#issuecomment-4488890811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119474","id":4488890811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC48Juw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-19T14:41:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T14:42:46Z","body":"> The save button should save the stats, and the print statement included in the save button code would leave you to believe that it is saving the correct values. (If you use a break point, you can see that it only saves default values. The print statement is misleading.)\n> The load button should bring up the saved values, instead, it only loads the current values in memory. There is a print statement that proves that it is clickable.\n\nI didn't check the project, but sounds like you are saving and loading a resource from the same path. If the resource is still in the memory, `load()` method will return that instance instead of a new one.\n\nEither make sure the references to the resource are released, load using CACHE_MODE_IGNORE_DEEP, or don't use Resources for saving.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4488890811/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]